        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                "word": "ivrognerie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cc859ec5-8bfe-44e9-9e85-70a9e5f77543",
                        "entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ivrogneries"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                        "entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Habitude de s’enivrer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b64f62ed-2128-4719-954a-c94f91a7bd90",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "D’autres alléguaient que le vice héréditaire de l’ivrognerie avait absorbé ses facultés, qui n’étaient déjà pas très brillantes, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a69a8bf-6b92-4f95-be0f-f20177c0ddb4",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "Au lieu de boire des canons de vin bleu ou de petits verres d’eau-de-vie, les paysans et les vendeuses d’herbes du marché prennent une bebida helada, qui ne leur coûte pas plus cher, et du moins ne leur trouble pas la cervelle et ne les abrutit pas. L’absence d’ivrognerie rend les gens du peuple bien supérieurs aux classes correspondantes dans nos pays prétendus civilisés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4f0c370-0f8f-47c4-89a4-c28361ef9499",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "Beaucoup de personnes me trouveront sans doute bien indulgent. “ Vous innocentez l’ivrognerie, vous réalisez la crapule. ”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7f1205a-c895-45a4-aa23-7de6931f2609",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "On peut donc continuer à boire de l'eau de Seltz sans crainte, […]. C'est un digestif, un stimulant de l'appétit, un philtre merveilleux qui donne à un vin médiocre les qualités d'un bon cru, et fait plus contre l’ivrognerie que toutes les Sociétés de tempérance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01ff75b7-b86c-4578-b5ba-54396ef49185",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "[…]: moi, ça me lève le cœur, des fois, cette ivrognerie de personnes de la société, vicieuses et sans aucune tenue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7231fd38-0738-4e8c-a11d-2b726ffc0099",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "Les personnes qu'on nous amène ivres mortes et que l’ivrognerie a rendues violentes sont encore plus pathétiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecbc09df-b205-4dc6-8970-f69cb1b3c7c9",
                                "sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                                "text": "Si le mot \"alcoolisme\" est la définition « usuelle », le terme \"œnolisme\" est une expression plus médicale et assez élégante, mais à la campagne, on appelle ça tout bonnement \"l’ivrognerie\".\nVoilà un mot qui dit ce qu'il veut dire !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "172577be-9fd9-4162-acf8-483a8486a9b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Trunksucht",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Trunksucht",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                        "entry_id": "3b48b271-1e6c-3609-a138-9ea8f3363187",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "zwanghafter Genuss alkoholischer Getränke"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52b73dce-91fa-4861-a2ed-74798ee44831",
                                                "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                                "text": "„Neben Klischees betonten die antiken Autoren gerne das Ungewöhnliche, Fremde und Exotische — so zum Beispiel die Trunksucht der Kelten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71be6093-487b-468c-8a16-031a42413387",
                                                "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                                "text": "„Denn die Kolonialherren sorgten auch für die Verbreitung von Trunksucht und Tripper.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5663e6e6-451a-463b-9bf7-f9ab1e42cf23",
                                                "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                                "text": "„Die Heilsarmee hat ein großes Arbeitsfeld in den Hafenstädten, um der Trunksucht und anderen Lastern entgegenzutreten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e0098a8-2674-4d71-8237-1993b57fe05c",
                                                "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                                "text": "„Platon missbilligt ihre Trunksucht; sein Schüler Aristoteles ist nicht weniger kritisch, er nennt sie unbeherrscht und unfähig zu staatlicher Ordnung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad116852-1d79-4bda-8b27-81db2daa8132",
                                                "sense_id": "eed8c19e-fe87-3b7c-a798-fdbab91aa6b3",
                                                "text": "„So bestand und bewährte sich unsere Freundschaft mehrere Jahre lang. In dieser Zeit aber hatte mein Charakter infolge meiner teuflischen Trunksucht – ich erröte bei diesem Bekenntnis – eine völlige Wandlung zum Bösen durchgemacht.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "63111ffe-d564-40e9-9fe6-0b30e2547864",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
                        "target_lang_word": "drunkenness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "drunkenness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f17732b2-78ee-3532-8571-21917930638e",
                                        "entry_id": "1042a7d3-6e4c-3b39-b4d7-74613176ba25",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of being drunk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "574bbc9e-455a-499d-8522-ff97ea27727f",
                                                "sense_id": "f17732b2-78ee-3532-8571-21917930638e",
                                                "text": "But presently the fumes of the wine rising to his head, he became helplessly drunk and his side-muscles and limbs relaxed and he swayed to and fro on my back. When I saw that he had lost his senses for drunkenness, I put my head to his legs and, loosing them from my neck, stooped down well-nigh to the ground and threw him at full length, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52bde6e9-85ff-477c-b8fa-ff4bcbdef3ad",
                                                "sense_id": "f17732b2-78ee-3532-8571-21917930638e",
                                                "text": "The Englishman had a reputation throughout Europe for gluttony; it was said that overeating was the English vice, just as lust was the French vice and drunkenness the German vice. Some Englishmen became very fat, and were famous for being so. Henry VIII ate enormous meals, but as a young man he was slim, perhaps because he always took a great deal of physical exercise. By the time that he was forty-five he was suffering from painful ulcers in his leg which prevented him from riding or walking without the greatest difficulty; but though he ceased to take exercise, he ate as much as ever. He then became very fat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7411738a-9f9d-42c2-9502-c7911f45866a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0e2777c-ba05-35c9-853b-2a7d8afdc9d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5efd521-4357-3cdb-ba36-3895a2d9aef7",
